src/pages/events/kennedy-center/2026-09-17-30-day-notice-before-demolition.astro:55:      <p class="railed rail-note" data-layer="fact">The federal docket's September 17 minute order was not available as a court-hosted document in the public sources we could preserve. UPI reproduces the operative sentence below in full. Beatty's counsel quotes part of it and describes the requirement as 30 days' advance warning; the surrounding motions, declarations, earlier opinions and board records are preserved separately.<Cite s="upi-kennedy-center-2026-09-17" passage="To avoid any confusion on that score given more recent events" /><Cite s="beatty-counsel-reaction-2026-09-17" passage="any changes to the scope of the project plans" /><Cite s="beatty-counsel-reaction-2026-09-17" passage="30 days’ advance warning" /></p>
src/pages/events/kennedy-center/2026-09-17-30-day-notice-before-demolition.astro-56-
src/pages/events/kennedy-center/2026-09-17-30-day-notice-before-demolition.astro-57-      <div data-layer="proof" class="event-record-context">
src/pages/events/kennedy-center/2026-09-17-30-day-notice-before-demolition.astro:58:        <p class="sources-line">This story rests on filings in Beatty v. Trump and D.C. Preservation League v. Trump; the court's May 29 opinions; the board's August meeting record; the August 28 joint report; the September 16 scheduling order; federal statutes governing the Kennedy Center; the September 17 minute order as reproduced in full by UPI and quoted in part by Beatty's counsel; and the coverage records checked against those documents.</p>
src/pages/events/kennedy-center/2026-09-17-30-day-notice-before-demolition.astro-59-      </div>
src/pages/events/kennedy-center/2026-09-17-30-day-notice-before-demolition.astro-60-
src/pages/events/kennedy-center/2026-09-17-30-day-notice-before-demolition.astro-61-      <section id="what-happened">
src/pages/events/kennedy-center/2026-09-17-30-day-notice-before-demolition.astro-62-        <p class="sec-kicker" data-layer="narrative">The request and the ruling</p>
src/pages/events/kennedy-center/2026-09-17-30-day-notice-before-demolition.astro-63-        <h2 data-layer="fact">The judge refused the hearing and added an advance-notice rule</h2>
--
src/pages/events/kennedy-center/2026-09-17-30-day-notice-before-demolition.astro-65-        <p data-layer="narrative">The filing also put two public signals before Cooper. Trump had told reporters that without recognition for his administration's role in the renovation and fundraising, the building would close and end up being ripped down. The filing included a photograph of him reading a placard that appeared to say “Kennedy Center DEMOLISHED.” ABC reported that the published images did not show the entire placard and that the visible word was cut off at “DEMOLIS.” A Kennedy Center spokesperson separately said that nothing was being demolished.<Cite s="beatty-notice-85-2026-09-17" /><Cite s="beatty-notice-85-2026-09-17" passage="it will end up being ripped down" /><Cite s="beatty-notice-85-2026-09-17" passage="appears to read “Kennedy Center DEMOLISHED.”" /><Cite s="abc-kennedy-center-2026-09-17" passage="The published images don't show the entire placard" /><Cite s="abc-kennedy-center-2026-09-17" passage="cut off as “DEMOLIS.”" /><Cite s="cbs-kennedy-center-2026-09-17" passage="nothing is being demolished" /></p>
src/pages/events/kennedy-center/2026-09-17-30-day-notice-before-demolition.astro-66-        <p data-layer="narrative">Cooper denied the hearing. He nevertheless ordered the defendants to give plaintiffs in both cases written notice before implementing a covered change.<Cite s="upi-kennedy-center-2026-09-17" passage="Beatty's request for a hearing was denied" /><Cite s="upi-kennedy-center-2026-09-17" passage="provide such notice in writing to Plaintiffs in both cases" /></p>
src/pages/events/kennedy-center/2026-09-17-30-day-notice-before-demolition.astro-67-        <QuoteCard speaker="U.S. District Judge Christopher Cooper" when="September 17, 2026" where="Minute order, as reproduced by UPI">
src/pages/events/kennedy-center/2026-09-17-30-day-notice-before-demolition.astro-68-          <p>To avoid any confusion on that score given more recent events, the Court hereby ORDERS Defendants [the Kennedy Center board] to provide such notice in writing to Plaintiffs in both cases more than 30 days before the implementation of any changes to the scope of the project plans presented to the Court in D.C. Preservation League [a separate case], including but not limited to any 'demolition' of the Center's main building.<Cite s="upi-kennedy-center-2026-09-17" passage="To avoid any confusion on that score given more recent events" /></p>
src/pages/events/kennedy-center/2026-09-17-30-day-notice-before-demolition.astro-69-        </QuoteCard>
src/pages/events/kennedy-center/2026-09-17-30-day-notice-before-demolition.astro:70:        <p data-layer="narrative">The order also required the administration to update Cooper by September 23 on the status of the temporary closure and emergency repairs.<Cite s="abc-kennedy-center-2026-09-17" passage="update him on the status of the" /><Cite s="abc-kennedy-center-2026-09-17" passage="emergency repairs" /> Beatty's counsel said Cooper “ordered discovery into the Board’s actions related to a potential demolition.”<Cite s="beatty-counsel-reaction-2026-09-17" passage="ordered discovery into the Board’s actions related to a potential demolition" /> UPI's reproduced order text contains the notice command but no discovery provision.<Cite s="upi-kennedy-center-2026-09-17" passage="the Court hereby ORDERS Defendants" /></p>
