e.g., Petties ex rel. Martin v. District of Columbia, 662 F.3d 564, 569 (D.C. Cir. 2011). The party

seeking dissolution “bears the burden of establishing that changed circumstances warrant relief.”

Talbott, 775 F. Supp. 3d at 449 (quoting Am. Council of the Blind, 878 F.3d at 366).

