I.     Summary Judgment Is Warranted on Plaintiff’s Outstanding Claims.

       The Court’s May 29, 2026 memorandum opinion provides the governing framework for

these combined motions and underscores why Defendants are now entitled to judgment as a matter

of law. Following that opinion and the Court’s contemporaneous Order, ECF No. 49, what remains

are Count Two and those portions of Counts Four, Five, and Seven related to the Board’s decision

to adopt an operational model that calls for the full, but temporary, closure of the Center. 8 See ECF

