conclusions can be drawn about the Board’s August and September 2026 votes. The record now

proves conclusively that, in independently considering newly defined operational proposals to

undertake remediation and restoration work, the Board has fully satisfied its fiduciary duties.

       Boards of trustees must operate under the “duties of participation and prudence, the latter

of which requires a trustee to ‘administer the trust as a prudent person would, in light of the

purposes, terms, and other circumstances of the trust.’ ” ECF No. 50 at 75 (quoting Restatement




